          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "**Track:** Middle Eastern & Mediterranean Folk | **Unit:** Comparative | **Tier:** 4"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Marketing labels flatten Turkey and sibling nations — trad is regional, not one sound."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "compared-with-turkey",
      "title": "Compared with Turkey",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Use the anchor nation as reference: when this lesson names a shared instrument or form, ask how practice differs by region and social context."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "key-points",
      "title": "Key points",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "- Regional labels are maps, not single repertoires.\n- Anchor unit provides depth; comparison adds precision.\n- Marketing often flattens specificity — compare recordings."
        }
      ]
    },
